<main id="main">
<section class="phero"><div class="phero-bg" data-parallax="0.15"><img src="/assets/img/photos/storm-supercell.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/storm-supercell-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/storm-supercell.webp 1024w" sizes="100vw" width="1024" height="682" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"></div><div class="wrap phero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><ol><li><a href="/">Home</a></li><li><a href="/counties-and-cities/">Counties &amp; cities</a></li><li aria-current="page">Oxford</li></ol></nav><p class="kicker">North Mississippi</p><h1>Claim Appraisal for Oxford Homes, Condos and Rentals</h1><p class="lede">Oxford has grown fast around the University of Mississippi, and a lot of its newer property is condos and rentals. When hail, wind or ice damages your Oxford property and the carrier underpays, appraisal can help settle the amount.</p><div class="btns"><a class="btn btn-gold" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> Call (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/talk-to-an-appraiser/">Free claim review</a></div><ul class="hero-facts"><li><small>County</small><b>Lafayette County</b></li><li><small>Region</small><b>North Mississippi</b></li><li><small>Inspections</small><b>On site</b></li></ul></div></section><div class="wrap cols"><article class="prose"><div class="glance">
<div><p class="glance-h">Neighborhoods &amp; areas</p><ul class="chips"><li>The Square</li><li>North Lamar</li><li>South Lamar</li><li>University Avenue</li><li>Grand Oaks</li><li>Taylor</li></ul></div>
<div><p class="glance-h">Housing mix</p><p>Oxford mixes older homes near the Square and campus, condo complexes and student rentals, newer single-family subdivisions, and rural homes across Lafayette County.</p></div>
<div><p class="glance-h">Storm history</p><ul class="storm-list"><li><b>Feb 1994</b><span>North Mississippi ice storm with massive tree and power-line damage</span></li><li><b>Feb 2021</b><span>Winter storm with ice, snow and burst pipes</span></li><li><b>Dec 2022</b><span>Hard freeze and frozen-pipe losses</span></li></ul></div>
<div><p class="glance-h">Local claim risks</p><ul class="chips chips-red"><li>Hail and straight-line wind</li><li>Tornadoes in spring storm systems</li><li>Ice storms and tree limb damage</li><li>Frozen pipes in rentals left empty over breaks</li><li>Water damage spreading between condo units</li></ul></div>
</div><h2>Oxford, Lafayette County and Ole Miss</h2>
<p>Oxford is the county seat of Lafayette County and home to the University of Mississippi. The courthouse Square sits at the center of town, with older homes along North and South Lamar and the streets running toward campus on University Avenue. Beyond that core, Oxford has added condo complexes, apartment-style rentals and subdivisions like Grand Oaks, while small communities such as Taylor sit just outside town.</p>
<p>That mix of property, much of it owned by people who don’t live in it full time, shapes the claims we see.</p>

<h2>Weather that drives Oxford claims</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Ice:</strong> the February 1994 ice storm coated North Mississippi and brought down trees and power lines for weeks. The February 2021 winter storm brought ice, snow and frozen pipes.</li>
<li><strong>Freeze:</strong> the December 2022 hard freeze hit during winter break, when many rentals and condos were empty.</li>
<li><strong>Hail and wind:</strong> spring storms bring hail, straight-line wind and occasional tornadoes across Lafayette County.</li>
</ul>
<p>Our guide to <a href="/claim-advice/ice-storm-tree-claims-north-mississippi/">ice storm and tree claims in North Mississippi</a> covers how those losses are usually handled.</p>

<h2>Condos, rentals and student housing</h2>
<h3>Who owns what</h3>
<p>In a condo, the association’s master policy and your unit-owner policy each cover part of the building. Read your declarations and bylaws to see where the line falls for walls, floors, cabinets and fixtures. When a pipe bursts upstairs and water runs through three units, each policy may produce its own estimate and its own dispute.</p>
<h3>Empty units and frozen pipes</h3>
<p>Many policies include conditions about maintaining heat in a vacant or unoccupied unit. Whether a freeze loss is covered is a coverage question, not an appraisal question. Once coverage is accepted, the scope of drying, tear-out and rebuild is fair game.</p>
<h3>Loss of rent and contents</h3>
<p>Landlord policies often include fair rental value coverage. Furnished rentals add a contents claim. Both can be underestimated when repairs drag on.</p>

<h2>Common estimate disputes in Oxford</h2>
<ul>
<li>Hail damage on condo roofs written as spot repairs across buildings that share one roof system.</li>
<li>Water losses scoped for one unit when moisture readings show it reached the units below.</li>
<li>Older homes near the Square priced with modern materials that don’t match the original trim and finishes.</li>
<li>Ice-related limb damage where the roof repair is approved but the gutter, fascia and siding work is left out.</li>
</ul>
<div class="callout"><b class="callout-t">HOAs and associations</b><p>An association disputing a master-policy claim follows its own policy’s appraisal clause. Our <a href="/our-appraisal-services/commercial-hoa-appraisal/">commercial and HOA appraisal</a> service handles association claims.</p></div>

<h2>How we can help</h2>
<p>Whether you live in Oxford year-round or own a rental from out of town, we can review your carrier’s estimate and, where your policy allows, represent you through appraisal. Start with the <a href="/our-appraisal-services/ice-storm-freeze-appraisal/">ice storm and freeze appraisal</a> service if your loss came from cold weather. Confirm any deadline with a Mississippi attorney.</p>
<h2>Appraisal services in Oxford</h2>
<p>Every Mississippi Insurance Appraiser service is available in Oxford and the rest of Lafayette County, including:</p>
<ul><li><a href="/our-appraisal-services/appraisal-demand-representation/">Appraisal Demand Representation</a></li><li><a href="/our-appraisal-services/home-insurance-appraisal/">Home Insurance Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/our-appraisal-services/commercial-hoa-appraisal/">Commercial &amp; HOA Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/our-appraisal-services/roof-hail-claim-appraisal/">Roof &amp; Hail Claim Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/our-appraisal-services/tornado-wind-damage-appraisal/">Tornado &amp; Wind Damage Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/our-appraisal-services/carrier-estimate-review/">Carrier Estimate Review</a></li></ul>
<h2>Oxford claim questions</h2><div class="faqs"><details><summary>I own a student rental in Oxford and live out of town. Can you still help?</summary><p>Yes. We can review the carrier’s estimate and handle the appraisal process with you remotely, coordinating access to the property as needed.</p></details><details><summary>A burst pipe damaged several condo units. Whose policy pays?</summary><p>That depends on the association’s master policy, your unit-owner policy and the condo documents. Appraisal does not decide which policy covers what, but it can settle the amount of loss under a policy once coverage is accepted.</p></details></div>
